culty/hard} :question/id #uuid "019711ee-80ff-5bba-9b3e-59b676517b88" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$\\{6x - 8y - 31 = 0; 2x - 4y - 6 = 0$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{6x - 8y - 31 = 0(1); 2x - 4y - 6 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2x - 4y - 6 &= 0 \\\\ 2x - 4y &= 6 \\\\ 2x &= 6 + 4y \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{6 + 4y}{2} \\\\ x &= 3 + 2y \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=3+2y$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 6x - 8y - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 6(3 + 2y) - 8y - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 18 + 12y - 8y - 31 &= 0 \\\\ -13 + 4y &= 0 \\\\ 4y &= 13 \\\\ y &= \\dfrac{13}{4} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{13}{4}\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 6x - 8y - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 6x - 8\\left(\\dfrac{13}{4}\\right) - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 6x - 26 - 31 &= 0 \\\\ 6x - 57 &= 0 \\\\ 6x &= 57 \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{19}{2} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=\\dfrac{19}{2}$ and\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{13}{4}\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{19}{2},\\dfrac{13}{4}\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf84d08-1dca-5218-a07d-994057aff387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 6, b = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505013} {:answer/id #uuid "528de811-2b56-5a74-8d2e-07cb5fc3b4d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = -11, b = -6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505027} {:answer/id #uuid "5db52a37-23c1-5600-9bdb-08a8c2b96623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 1, b = 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505030} {:answer/id #uuid "c22e9a45-ce60-5743-bfae-86b5026038eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 31, b = 36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505065} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b41247-404b-570f-87a4-1f5c8538e314" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = -\\dfrac{27}{5}, b = \\dfrac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5db52a37-23c1-5600-9bdb-08a8c2b96623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a = 1, b = 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505030} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a812c87-5420-54d1-b5e9-1d7596284773" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "037d812f-9cb8-5f58-959c-05369edfd299" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$\\{7a - 8b + 41 = 0; 4a - 4b + 20 = 0$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{7a - 8b + 41 = 0(1); 4a - 4b + 20 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $a$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4a - 4b + 20 &= 0 \\\\ 4a - 4b &= -20 \\\\ 4a &= -20 + 4b \\\\ a &= \\dfrac{-20 + 4b}{4} \\\\ a &= -5 + b \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $a=-5+b$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 7a - 8b + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 7(-5 + b) - 8b + 41 &= 0 \\\\ -35 + 7b - 8b + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 6 - b &= 0 \\\\ -b &= -6 \\\\ b &= 6 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\nb=6\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $a$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 7a - 8b + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 7a - 8\\left(6\\right) + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 7a - 48 + 41 &= 0 \\\\ 7a - 7 &= 0 \\\\ 7a &= 7 \\\\ a &= 1 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=1$ and\n\n$$\nb=6\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(1,6\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e7cdf5a-5a46-5390-8a6a-5ed18ae9d9f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -1, y = -5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505018} {:answer/id #uuid "49c9a908-228f-59d5-8607-095ccbac281a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -8, y = 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505023} {:answer/id #uuid "7101e81a-dd60-5923-8f05-ece2ae2d5dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -5, y = -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505039} {:answer/id #uuid "d9612a71-c4c9-5df6-a1f8-4d50c4e71893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{5}{2}, y = -12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505076} {:answer/id #uuid "de10306a-4f55-5205-b610-875a785ea3d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 2, y = -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e7cdf5a-5a46-5390-8a6a-5ed18ae9d9f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -1, y = -5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505018} :answer-field/id #uuid "f40c9b80-4cc9-5cb8-afa4-0371d87b467c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505088}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b3f4cbe-31b3-5a2d-8c6e-81aafdba130b" :question/problem "Using the method of substitution, find the solution of\n$\\{2x + y = -7; 2x - 3y = 13$." :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{2x + y + 7 = 0(1); 2x - 3y - 13 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(1)$, we can solve for $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} y + 2x + 7 &= 0 \\\\ y + 2x &= -7 \\\\ y &= -7 - 2x \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=-7-2x$ into equation $\\color{red}(2)$ and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -3y + 2x - 13 &= 0 \\\\ -3(-7 - 2x) + 2x - 13 &= 0 \\\\ 21 + 6x + 2x - 13 &= 0 \\\\ 8 + 8x &= 0 \\\\ 8x &= -8 \\\\ x &= -1 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\nx=-1\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(2)$, then we can find the value of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -3y + 2x - 13 &= 0 \\\\ -3y + 2\\left(-1\\right) - 13 &= 0 \\\\ -3y - 2 - 13 &= 0 \\\\ -3y - 15 &= 0 \\\\ -3y &= 15 \\\\ y &= -5 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $y=-5$ and\n\n$$\nx=-1\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(-1,-5\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "188de890-3550-53a3-ae4b-7aee43ba4d4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = -\\dfrac{4}{5}, q = \\dfrac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505012} {:answer/id #uuid "6d5479ec-6dd9-59aa-b198-6622d2186e70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = -\\dfrac{8}{3}, q = \\dfrac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505037} {:answer/id #uuid "763b7950-8d3e-5755-9ce3-f22e1857cbd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = -2, q = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505041} {:answer/id #uuid "8bda9132-2104-519c-bd63-9eff3522c541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 4, q = -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505046} {:answer/id #uuid "92428644-31eb-5e54-8fc9-5cbb8799e701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 12, q = -10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bda9132-2104-519c-bd63-9eff3522c541" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 4, q = -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505046} :answer-field/id #uuid "6480680a-dfdb-5493-b635-b28d00002259" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0bd6815d-c6b1-5fc3-bc01-5728aba3b215" :question/problem "Using the method of substitution, find the solution of\n\n$\\{-6p - 9q = -6; 3p + 3q = 6$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{-6p - 9q + 6 = 0(1); 3p + 3q - 6 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $q$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3q + 3p - 6 &= 0 \\\\ 3q + 3p &= 6 \\\\ 3q &= 6 - 3p \\\\ q &= \\dfrac{6 - 3p}{3} \\\\ q &= 2 - p \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $q=2-p$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $p$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -9q - 6p + 6 &= 0 \\\\ -9(2 - p) - 6p + 6 &= 0 \\\\ -18 + 9p - 6p + 6 &= 0 \\\\ -12 + 3p &= 0 \\\\ 3p &= 12 \\\\ p &= 4 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\np=4\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $q$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -9q - 6p + 6 &= 0 \\\\ -9q - 6\\left(4\\right) + 6 &= 0 \\\\ -9q - 24 + 6 &= 0 \\\\ -9q - 18 &= 0 \\\\ -9q &= 18 \\\\ q &= -2 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $q=-2$ and\n\n$$\np=4\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(4,-2\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505044 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c604f56b-d302-58fb-a478-e6f140d1b44c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = -\\dfrac{19}{2}, q = \\dfrac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505069} {:answer/id #uuid "da8467be-0482-564f-b5d2-bfa6c1d51cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = -28, q = -25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505077} {:answer/id #uuid "dc3fef8b-68b3-5b51-aacc-bac81739ded6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = -8, q = 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505078} {:answer/id #uuid "eae0b3dd-9a86-5ad5-b884-59fe84fe608a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 47, q = -50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505082} {:answer/id #uuid "f1650eb8-3447-5c6d-a2aa-b63c52cf1523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 5, q = -8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc3fef8b-68b3-5b51-aacc-bac81739ded6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = -8, q = 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505078} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f45a298-4422-5551-8d83-c2422dc2c4cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "81d33e45-12e7-5f43-864d-1ce259421c85" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$\\{6p - 4q + 68 = 0; 4p + 4q + 12 = 0$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{6p - 4q + 68 = 0(1); 4p + 4q + 12 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $p$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4p + 4q + 12 &= 0 \\\\ 4p + 4q &= -12 \\\\ 4p &= -12 - 4q \\\\ p &= \\dfrac{-12 - 4q}{4} \\\\ p &= -3 - q \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=-3-q$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $q$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 6p - 4q + 68 &= 0 \\\\ 6(-3 - q) - 4q + 68 &= 0 \\\\ -18 - 6q - 4q + 68 &= 0 \\\\ 50 - 10q &= 0 \\\\ -10q &= -50 \\\\ q &= 5 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\nq=5\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $p$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 6p - 4q + 68 &= 0 \\\\ 6p - 4\\left(5\\right) + 68 &= 0 \\\\ 6p - 20 + 68 &= 0 \\\\ 6p + 48 &= 0 \\\\ 6p &= -48 \\\\ p &= -8 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=-8$ and\n\n$$\nq=5\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(-8,5\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505050 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1603d82b-c052-55fd-9a55-a364ff5e2cfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{13}{3}, y = -\\dfrac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505010} {:answer/id #uuid "1e963105-b7e6-5546-8c58-b81dea275cfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 5, y = -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505015} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d4ad7d-f15c-5de6-af54-c7b851da7a3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{13}{7}, y = \\dfrac{27}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505055} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4cd44a-762e-558f-bf0a-b46105f41178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 13, y = -11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505083} {:answer/id #uuid "ef570589-6178-5d0b-a363-96472e39717a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -\\dfrac{7}{3}, y = \\dfrac{13}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1603d82b-c052-55fd-9a55-a364ff5e2cfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{13}{3}, y = -\\dfrac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505010} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d8dbb77-04a8-5b1a-a763-3af48c384109" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505047}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "94502529-f765-562b-a0a6-063708d3571d" :question/problem "Using the method of substitution, find the solution of\n\n$\\{5x + 2y = 17; 3x + 3y = 6$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{5x + 2y - 17 = 0(1); 3x + 3y - 6 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3y + 3x - 6 &= 0 \\\\ 3y + 3x &= 6 \\\\ 3y &= 6 - 3x \\\\ y &= \\dfrac{6 - 3x}{3} \\\\ y &= 2 - x \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=2-x$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2y + 5x - 17 &= 0 \\\\ 2(2 - x) + 5x - 17 &= 0 \\\\ 4 - 2x + 5x - 17 &= 0 \\\\ -13 + 3x &= 0 \\\\ 3x &= 13 \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{13}{3} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{13}{3}\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2y + 5x - 17 &= 0 \\\\ 2y + 5\\left(\\dfrac{13}{3}\\right) - 17 &= 0 \\\\ 2y + \\dfrac{65}{3} - 17 &= 0 \\\\ 2y + \\dfrac{14}{3} &= 0 \\\\ 2y &= -\\dfrac{14}{3} \\\\ y &= -\\dfrac{7}{3} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $y=-\\dfrac{7}{3}$ and\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{13}{3}\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{13}{3},-\\dfrac{7}{3}\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505053 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f359dcf-82e1-573f-b829-c73044894a0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 61, q = -32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505007} {:answer/id #uuid "4324f3ee-42a2-5b81-af28-c33a37b544cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 1, q = -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505019} {:answer/id #uuid "c8880a82-ecf0-5fd0-98a4-687161107483" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = -2, q = 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505070} {:answer/id #uuid "f51c7ec6-517a-52a1-9d66-f23ef39a1baf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = -\\dfrac{13}{8}, q = -\\dfrac{11}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505089} {:answer/id #uuid "f6387b29-e54c-5f2f-b499-866421947cd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 5, q = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4324f3ee-42a2-5b81-af28-c33a37b544cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "p = 1, q = -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505019} :answer-field/id #uuid "495cde91-9097-5016-a4b7-f83c157183cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505022}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a20b2f41-8f60-5daf-a6d6-584b1826ccc0" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$\\{-6p + 4q + 14 = 0; 2p + 4q + 6 = 0$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{-6p + 4q + 14 = 0(1); 2p + 4q + 6 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $p$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2p + 4q + 6 &= 0 \\\\ 2p + 4q &= -6 \\\\ 2p &= -6 - 4q \\\\ p &= \\dfrac{-6 - 4q}{2} \\\\ p &= -3 - 2q \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=-3-2q$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $q$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -6p + 4q + 14 &= 0 \\\\ -6(-3 - 2q) + 4q + 14 &= 0 \\\\ 18 + 12q + 4q + 14 &= 0 \\\\ 32 + 16q &= 0 \\\\ 16q &= -32 \\\\ q &= -2 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\nq=-2\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $p$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -6p + 4q + 14 &= 0 \\\\ -6p + 4\\left(-2\\right) + 14 &= 0 \\\\ -6p - 8 + 14 &= 0 \\\\ -6p + 6 &= 0 \\\\ -6p &= -6 \\\\ p &= 1 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $p=1$ and\n\n$$\nq=-2\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(1,-2\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505059 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "183f9a92-7d85-53ba-bb28-1b66842b5e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505011} {:answer/id #uuid "621871e5-d472-56df-b867-bc30be73a084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505032} {:answer/id #uuid "7639d21a-e892-5043-9cbc-a4fb6a9ca3a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505040} {:answer/id #uuid "a3410dfa-f1bf-5787-ac89-c05bbe4fd261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505054} {:answer/id #uuid "aecd726c-29f3-5f8c-8f56-bc34d79630a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3410dfa-f1bf-5787-ac89-c05bbe4fd261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505054} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2ae802f-7984-5f66-a194-5b364b61a802" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505066}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b1972fab-2da0-5ed8-b4bc-94b1335dd7b8" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $p - q$?\n\n$\\{2q + 16 = 0; 2p + 4q + 28 = 0$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{red}(1)$, we can solve for $q$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2q + 16 &= 0 \\\\ 2q &= -16 \\\\ q &= -8 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $q=-8$ into equation $\\color{blue}(2)$ and solve for $p$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2p + 4q + 28 &= 0 \\\\ 2p + 4\\left(-8\\right) + 28 &= 0 \\\\ 2p - 32 + 28 &= 0 \\\\ 2p &= 4 \\\\ p &= 2 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p - q = 2 - \\left(-8\\right) = 10$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95af81eb-d92c-51f4-b179-301af6b7074e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u = \\dfrac{11}{2}, v = -\\dfrac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505051} {:answer/id #uuid "acfc8fb0-a632-5e16-b446-56652d5a4097" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u = -20, v = 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505057} {:answer/id #uuid "d12356d8-5f09-5550-afeb-6ee5bf015a42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u = -\\dfrac{3}{4}, v = \\dfrac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505072} {:answer/id #uuid "d3311c96-9043-5bf6-8985-20298f056af3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u = -2, v = -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505073} {:answer/id #uuid "d8b07d76-38ae-5c13-9594-deedf6c03d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u = \\dfrac{13}{2}, v = -\\dfrac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95af81eb-d92c-51f4-b179-301af6b7074e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u = \\dfrac{11}{2}, v = -\\dfrac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505051} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fcd3ce7-5c00-5602-9356-92e21937475d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505052}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bc541194-7b78-5e2b-bcbd-7b99ad0d6b55" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$\\{3u - 10v - 24 = 0; 2u + 4v - 8 = 0$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{3u - 10v - 24 = 0(1); 2u + 4v - 8 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $u$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2u + 4v - 8 &= 0 \\\\ 2u + 4v &= 8 \\\\ 2u &= 8 - 4v \\\\ u &= \\dfrac{8 - 4v}{2} \\\\ u &= 4 - 2v \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $u=4-2v$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $v$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3u - 10v - 24 &= 0 \\\\ 3(4 - 2v) - 10v - 24 &= 0 \\\\ 12 - 6v - 10v - 24 &= 0 \\\\ -12 - 16v &= 0 \\\\ -16v &= 12 \\\\ v &= -\\dfrac{3}{4} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\nv=-\\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $u$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3u - 10v - 24 &= 0 \\\\ 3u - 10\\left(-\\dfrac{3}{4}\\right) - 24 &= 0 \\\\ 3u + \\dfrac{15}{2} - 24 &= 0 \\\\ 3u - \\dfrac{33}{2} &= 0 \\\\ 3u &= \\dfrac{33}{2} \\\\ u &= \\dfrac{11}{2} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=\\dfrac{11}{2}$ and\n\n$$\nv=-\\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{11}{2},-\\dfrac{3}{4}\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505067 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f226940-943f-583c-bfad-7e0e457a4495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -2, y = 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505006} {:answer/id #uuid "555ddb93-7974-58de-ab26-661f601b92e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 8, y = -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505028} {:answer/id #uuid "64401688-65df-53f3-8d39-351c9d9e6764" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 40, y = -18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505033} {:answer/id #uuid "6e4da099-0ce4-5de2-b9ea-a991cd983ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{152}{9}, y = -\\dfrac{58}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505038} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7e8244-2976-579c-bc22-7eba63d1400a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{16}{3}, y = \\dfrac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "555ddb93-7974-58de-ab26-661f601b92e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 8, y = -2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505028} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e4dec55-ce2d-5af5-9a72-496c649ac130" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505026}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c436498f-fd9e-57ef-8d83-36d474017d7b" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$\\{-9x - 9y + 54 = 0; 4x + 8y - 16 = 0$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{-9x - 9y + 54 = 0(1); 4x + 8y - 16 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4x + 8y - 16 &= 0 \\\\ 4x + 8y &= 16 \\\\ 4x &= 16 - 8y \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{16 - 8y}{4} \\\\ x &= 4 - 2y \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=4-2y$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -9x - 9y + 54 &= 0 \\\\ -9(4 - 2y) - 9y + 54 &= 0 \\\\ -36 + 18y - 9y + 54 &= 0 \\\\ 18 + 9y &= 0 \\\\ 9y &= -18 \\\\ y &= -2 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\ny=-2\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -9x - 9y + 54 &= 0 \\\\ -9x - 9\\left(-2\\right) + 54 &= 0 \\\\ -9x + 18 + 54 &= 0 \\\\ -9x + 72 &= 0 \\\\ -9x &= -72 \\\\ x &= 8 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=8$ and\n\n$$\ny=-2\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(8,-2\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505080 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21558f44-0dc3-5110-86d8-087739b963cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 7, y = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505016} {:answer/id #uuid "2a2a695b-0075-5418-984a-73a32e5438c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 2, y = 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505017} {:answer/id #uuid "5ddccadf-36b4-5cfb-b0ee-35c46f4f5a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{85}{7}, y = \\dfrac{32}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505031} {:answer/id #uuid "c0951927-a913-5192-9133-898c36910349" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{13}{3}, y = -\\dfrac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505064} {:answer/id #uuid "f38326ee-5794-566c-b7a6-3ec481868125" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 31, y = 14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21558f44-0dc3-5110-86d8-087739b963cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 7, y = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505016} :answer-field/id #uuid "8913c7f5-e0f0-50ed-8a31-fc8d655919b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e37d0a68-8577-5a70-a5bd-f408d06259f5" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$\\{7x - 7y - 35 = 0; 2x - 4y - 6 = 0$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{7x - 7y - 35 = 0(1); 2x - 4y - 6 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2x - 4y - 6 &= 0 \\\\ 2x - 4y &= 6 \\\\ 2x &= 6 + 4y \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{6 + 4y}{2} \\\\ x &= 3 + 2y \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=3+2y$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 7x - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7(3 + 2y) - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 21 + 14y - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ -14 + 7y &= 0 \\\\ 7y &= 14 \\\\ y &= 2 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\ny=2\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 7x - 7y - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7x - 7\\left(2\\right) - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7x - 14 - 35 &= 0 \\\\ 7x - 49 &= 0 \\\\ 7x &= 49 \\\\ x &= 7 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=7$ and\n\n$$\ny=2\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(7,2\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505081 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05d9c1d8-7776-59ee-ab3f-0c7ec5d99ad7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505003} {:answer/id #uuid "44ac7e7a-8cd6-5536-adaf-69acb445a0a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\dfrac{37}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505021} {:answer/id #uuid "4d5e58df-d87a-5d3b-8451-91e9e3f1757c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505025} {:answer/id #uuid "77b69005-e991-580b-b25e-307a1dd218c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505042} {:answer/id #uuid "92ad25d7-c40d-5066-bdbf-dd1acaadfdab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505049}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77b69005-e991-580b-b25e-307a1dd218c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505042} :answer-field/id #uuid "64e915ee-d4a5-507a-aa63-39fcbb83ebee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7e74981-78de-5721-8c70-6b15d18904de" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{4b + 32 = 0; 5a + 2b - 19 = 0$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{red}(1)$, we can solve for $b$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4b + 32 &= 0 \\\\ 4b &= -32 \\\\ b &= -8 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=-8$ into equation $\\color{blue}(2)$ and solve for $a$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 5a + 2b - 19 &= 0 \\\\ 5a + 2\\left(-8\\right) - 19 &= 0 \\\\ 5a - 16 - 19 &= 0 \\\\ 5a &= 35 \\\\ a &= 7 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a - b = 7 - \\left(-8\\right) = 15$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186505084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4352698-7af7-5d74-9c3a-0f951c3e6078" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Challenging System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c15ecbe-d346-5f65-915b-40b893526bce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -62, y = 33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505014} {:answer/id #uuid "66049ae6-acb9-5ef1-9cbf-b5980d95fb61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{9}{5}, y = -\\dfrac{11}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505036} {:answer/id #uuid "b8dc18ed-b3e2-5fe6-9ed6-a243f631ece2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{33}{10}, y = -\\dfrac{13}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505061} {:answer/id #uuid "bcc54da3-d9e3-59a1-99b4-05f22aa87741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\dfrac{31}{5}, y = -\\dfrac{11}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505063} {:answer/id #uuid "fab16b5f-e937-5c12-9738-1fe6637231e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -\\dfrac{13}{5}, y = \\dfrac{33}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505091}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fab16b5f-e937-5c12-9738-1fe6637231e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = -\\dfrac{13}{5}, y = \\dfrac{33}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505091} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac43374e-aef2-5557-9421-83f8f3b1b206" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ed97dc9b-b6f4-5076-b3bb-6acac17b72a7" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$\\{-10x - 10y + 7 = 0; 4x + 8y - 16 = 0$" :question/worked-solution "Sometimes, it's handy to assign a number to each equation in a system, so that we can refer to them more easily:\n\n$$\n\\{-10x - 10y + 7 = 0(1); 4x + 8y - 16 = 0(2)\n$$\n\nWe will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. Using equation $\\color{blue}(2)$, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 4x + 8y - 16 &= 0 \\\\ 4x + 8y &= 16 \\\\ 4x &= 16 - 8y \\\\ x &= \\dfrac{16 - 8y}{4} \\\\ x &= 4 - 2y \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=4-2y$ into equation $\\color{red}(1)$ and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -10x - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10(4 - 2y) - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -40 + 20y - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -33 + 10y &= 0 \\\\ 10y &= 33 \\\\ y &= \\dfrac{33}{10} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{33}{10}\n$$\n\ninto equation $\\color{red}(1)$, then we can find the value of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -10x - 10y + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10x - 10\\left(\\dfrac{33}{10}\\right) + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10x - 33 + 7 &= 0 \\\\ -10x - 26 &= 0 \\\\ -10x &= 26 \\\\ x &= -\\dfrac{13}{5} \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\dfrac{13}{5}$ and\n\n$$\ny=\\dfrac{33}{10}\n$$\n\n, which can be written as\n\n$$\n\\left(-\\dfrac{13}{5},\\dfrac{33}{10}\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508171 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8c7e85-9744-56b8-ad17-eac57676bf8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508177} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad2f379-b802-5a78-8607-922e2d09a5cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508211} {:answer/id #uuid "8c480585-9da5-5f00-8620-6f9f4b8471e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508212} {:answer/id #uuid "eda2dc78-3b71-5603-99bc-d2a18246622d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508237} {:answer/id #uuid "f85f3e50-67d1-5429-9721-b01c743f8a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f85f3e50-67d1-5429-9721-b01c743f8a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508239} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f3454ce-d4fe-5e69-9c29-1cf7c10c083c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01d4210c-99cb-5509-8003-8615f9f2d644" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{3a-3b=-18; -2a+b=7$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a+b & =7 \\\\ b & =7+2a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=7+2a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-3b & =-18 \\\\ 3a-3(7+2a) & =-18 \\\\ 3a-21-6a & =-18 \\\\ -3a-21 & =-18 \\\\ -3a & =3 \\\\ a & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-1$ into $b=7+2a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =7+2(-1) \\\\ b & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-1-(5)=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d173c13-b0d2-5277-871e-ecb5b39a99ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d173c13-b0d2-5277-871e-ecb5b39a99ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508176} :answer-field/id #uuid "4806076d-709c-5c2f-9105-4634d0972c75" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508191} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cea1815-2688-56a2-b4ab-965679af5b0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cea1815-2688-56a2-b4ab-965679af5b0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508175} :answer-field/id #uuid "aeabe89b-5ecb-5574-b4fc-226f206baafd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508225}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1814dd75-6dc3-5a88-93bf-56fa1a5ec858" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$\\{x+5y=21; y=x-3$\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.The solution is\n$($\n{{field-1}}\n$, $\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nNotice that the second equation is already solved for $y:$\n\n$$\ny=x-3\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $y$ in the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5y & =21 \\\\ x+5(x-3) & =21 \\\\ x+5x-15 & =21 \\\\ 6x-15 & =21 \\\\ 6x & =36 \\\\ x & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=6$ into $y=x-3,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(6)-3 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=6,\\,y=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70c5addc-2f92-5b2d-9cb9-315d42c2eaf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508203} {:answer/id #uuid "9c57a785-864f-578d-a998-d06a760a82b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508219} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc1215d-6449-5646-8c6a-c29cc1fa3226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508220} {:answer/id #uuid "a49ee6a6-f0da-5faa-b3bf-a70649b568f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508223} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6e4596-9bcf-59c6-a3cb-0242f006b8e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a49ee6a6-f0da-5faa-b3bf-a70649b568f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508223} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6ff3c1c-579d-56f9-8656-874b7f2727c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508232}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e8faafd-e3ef-5205-a5d6-b458af26d97f" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{-3a-2b=2; -3a+b=8$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a+b & =8 \\\\ b & =8+3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=8+3a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a-2b & =2 \\\\ -3a-2(8+3a) & =2 \\\\ -3a-16-6a & =2 \\\\ -9a-16 & =2 \\\\ -9a & =18 \\\\ a & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=-2$ into $b=8+3a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =8+3(-2) \\\\ b & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=-2-(2)=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508187 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3eb5050b-2f97-532e-b6c8-5866bcc9fa51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3eb5050b-2f97-532e-b6c8-5866bcc9fa51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508188} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac08740b-e844-58dd-baf4-40ef0b885178" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508224} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f39f41a-cfb3-5bf0-b58f-8d17841342c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f39f41a-cfb3-5bf0-b58f-8d17841342c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{17}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508189} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa771fca-d97d-5b82-add7-3f2815e11284" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3db3cd07-1246-5ea5-a44f-5fee48dd9a13" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$\\{3x+3y=2; 3x+y=-5$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y & =-5 \\\\ y & =-5-3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=-5-3x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+3y & =2 \\\\ 3x+3(-5-3x) & =2 \\\\ 3x-15-9x & =2 \\\\ -6x-15 & =2 \\\\ -6x & =17 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{17}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=-\\frac{17}{6}$ into $y=-5-3x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5-3(-\\frac{17}{6}) \\\\ y & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\frac{17}{6},\\,y=\\frac{7}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508204 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61123492-b1fa-52ea-a78d-92d15eb4799a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61123492-b1fa-52ea-a78d-92d15eb4799a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508201} :answer-field/id #uuid "00e813eb-39d3-591a-bc56-b776bdfd2316" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508170} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fc36be2-1ad6-5b03-b736-d29211c26e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fc36be2-1ad6-5b03-b736-d29211c26e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508194} :answer-field/id #uuid "84b6ed04-ec34-5023-a363-127985a3747a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "76c476e0-406c-5751-a806-f5cbe03fe610" :question/problem "Find the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$\\{-3x+4y=8; -2x+y=6$\n\nThe solution is $($ {{field-1}} $, $ {{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+y & =6 \\\\ y & =6+2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $y=6+2x$ into the first equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+4y & =8 \\\\ -3x+4(6+2x) & =8 \\\\ -3x+24+8x & =8 \\\\ 5x+24 & =8 \\\\ 5x & =-16 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{16}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $x=-\\frac{16}{5}$ into $y=6+2x,$ we can then find the value of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =6+2(-\\frac{16}{5}) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-\\frac{16}{5},\\,y=-\\frac{2}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b524116-52f0-5f16-ae76-c059374938ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508185} {:answer/id #uuid "7be0167d-61f1-500e-a6e6-d5a8f953e8c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508206} {:answer/id #uuid "904ce195-1201-5ff2-98fd-a1b9b5f6be03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508213} {:answer/id #uuid "979f6cea-60ca-5f62-beef-5756f8383e4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508217} {:answer/id #uuid "cfb36f0e-5371-55ee-b6e5-d11c77737dc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b524116-52f0-5f16-ae76-c059374938ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508185} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a85b03b-c3ea-57e4-a844-98bb80d07f7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7afeeb08-8b8f-54f1-86b4-033f592e20d8" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $a - b$?\n\n$\\{-5a+2b=9; -3a+b=3$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the second equation, we can isolate $b$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3a+b & =3 \\\\ b & =3+3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $b=3+3a$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5a+2b & =9 \\\\ -5a+2(3+3a) & =9 \\\\ -5a+6+6a & =9 \\\\ a+6 & =9 \\\\ a & =3 \\\\ a & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $a=3$ into $b=3+3a,$ we can then find the value of $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =3+3(3) \\\\ b & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a-b=3-(12)=-9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073752 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e79a91b-c479-53da-9f06-59c082fa4187" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Linear Equations Using Substitution" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048826 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Equations by Substitution"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32fad7a2-8a24-54a3-82c3-95bdccedab06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508183} {:answer/id #uuid "55557865-d7a4-5c61-a72d-2df58ccc52f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508196} {:answer/id #uuid "568a98b9-849b-5575-92e8-a07c6266f271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508197} {:answer/id #uuid "afc824e1-f2ad-5146-9402-020f186abb13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508226} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4128bc-2e10-521b-aec7-327b7f86a452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afc824e1-f2ad-5146-9402-020f186abb13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508226} :answer-field/id #uuid "2074e8b8-4078-53a4-973e-82b464298bff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c5faa09-66e6-54c1-b548-04286527c92b" :question/problem "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $p - q$?\n\n$\\{4p=-24; p+5q=19$" :question/worked-solution "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. \n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $p$ by dividing both sides by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4p & =-24 \\\\ p & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $p=-6$ into the second equation and solve for $q:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p+5q & =19 \\\\ (-6)+5q & =19 \\\\ 5q & =25 \\\\ q & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p-q=-6-(5)=-11.$"}]}
